## OBJECTION 1 (para 5, markers ['CLM-001', 'CLM-002', 'CLM-003', 'CLM-004', 'tantrasara-a08:tsa08-p03', 'tsa-a08-v55', 'tsa-a08-v56'])

## OBJECTION
The claim fails at the locator level before it reaches doctrinal plausibility. CLM-001, CLM-002, CLM-003, CLM-004, tsa-a08-v55, and tsa-a08-v56 all have “no formal entry” in the banked evidence. The under-test claims are marked (R); R never promotes itself, and here there is no T entry to promote them. The Sanskrit renderings in CLM-003/004 are therefore not banked evidence at all. The strongest counter-reading is: the T material supports a mixed reckoning of five kañcukas plus Māyā as a distinct covering/category, and a Māyā-person ladder; it does not support a clean formal equation “Māyā-six = six sheaths named,” nor the v56 gloss “awareness set aside; kalā falling above stands sheath-like.” `TattvaInventory.lean :: maya_six_count` is MODEL/CONTEXT_ONLY: it says 8.55 “describes six coverings starting with māyā” and “checks the candidate list,” not that the candidate is proved. Treating that as confirmation would be exactly the R-to-T self-promotion the destroy pass forbids.

## What-banked-sources-say
- `tantrasara-a08:tsa08-p03`: T entries are pinned, but they do not contain CLM-001–004. `Pramatr.lean :: seven` supports “Māyā-person ladder; vijñānākala above Māyā; mala-person→Śiva-equality”—not “six sheaths named.”
- `Kancuka.lean :: count_5` is the closest support: “kañcuka-six reckoning; five + māyā (mixed reckonings recorded).” At most this supports a six-item reckoning under mixed accounting; it does not license “Māyā-six = six sheaths named” or the verse translations.
- `Kancuka.lean :: pairings_distinct` gives kalā→partial agency, rāga functions, kāla/niyati delimiting, but explicitly notes “pairing gloss itself R.” So the structural side is banked; the gloss is not.
